Notes:
* While E has accent material and two different colors, it only has one primary material.
**F is allowed under current code, as current code states that ‘any primary material may be used as a
secondary material’, and does not prevent primary materials from covering 100% of the façade. The
proposed code amendment would not allow this building as material variation is required (proposed
language: “No one primary material may cover more than 70% of the facades”).

Also, a few people stated they did not have time to take the survey, and two stated they had no
preference when it came to the look of apartment buildings in Cheyenne.

It is understood that the sample size, timing, location, and frequency of the outreach makes the results
non-scientific, but this outreach is better than no outreach at all.

The response for finding E desirable while the rejecting G and C may speak to a preference for the
horizontal massing, vertical massing, or other element not directly related to materials (requirements
for open space of this nature can be found in sections of 6.6.4.b).
